    {
      "day": "2026-11-11",
      "room": "all",
      "type": "social",
      "start": "17:00",
      "end": "18:30",
      "title": "Group 1: Pupi · Group 2: Train",
      "description": "Participants are split into two groups. From 17:00 to 18:30 Group 1 attends the puppet show and Group 2 takes the train ride; from 18:30 to 20:00 they swap.\n\nOpera dei Pupi – Sicilian puppet theatre\nA traditional show of the Opera dei Pupi, Sicily's marionette theatre, recognised by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Hand-carved puppets in shining armour, moved from above with iron rods, act out the adventures of Charlemagne's paladins – Orlando, Rinaldo and their duels with the Saracens – while the puppeteers give voice to every character.\n\nOrtigia by tourist train\nA ride around Ortigia, the island that is the historic heart of Siracusa and part of a UNESCO World Heritage site: the Temple of Apollo, Piazza Duomo and the cathedral built into a Greek temple, the Fountain of Arethusa and the waterfront along the old sea walls."
    },
    {
      "day": "2026-11-11",
      "room": "all",
      "type": "social",
      "start": "18:30",
      "end": "20:00",
      "title": "Group 1: Train · Group 2: Pupi",
      "description": "Second round: from 18:30 to 20:00 Group 1 takes the train ride and Group 2 attends the puppet show.\n\nOpera dei Pupi – Sicilian puppet theatre\nA traditional show of the Opera dei Pupi, Sicily's marionette theatre, recognised by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Hand-carved puppets in shining armour, moved from above with iron rods, act out the adventures of Charlemagne's paladins – Orlando, Rinaldo and their duels with the Saracens – while the puppeteers give voice to every character.\n\nOrtigia by tourist train\nA ride around Ortigia, the island that is the historic heart of Siracusa and part of a UNESCO World Heritage site: the Temple of Apollo, Piazza Duomo and the cathedral built into a Greek temple, the Fountain of Arethusa and the waterfront along the old sea walls."
    },
